<article class="env-remark" id="09Z3">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09Z3">Remark <span data-tag="09Z3">59.55.6</span>.</a> In the situation of Lemma <a href="/tag/09Z2" data-tag="09Z2">59.55.5</a> if $\mathcal{G}$ is a sheaf of sets on $Y_{\acute{e}tale}$, then we have </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \Gamma (Y, \mathcal{G}) = \text{Equalizer}( \xymatrix{ \Gamma (X_0, f_0^{-1}\mathcal{G}) \ar@<1ex>[r] \ar@<-1ex>[r] &  \Gamma (X_1, f_1^{-1}\mathcal{G}) } )  \]
</div>
  <p> This is proved in exactly the same way, by showing that the sheaf $\mathcal{G}$ is the equalizer of the two maps $f_{0, *}f_0^{-1}\mathcal{G} \to f_{1, *}f_1^{-1}\mathcal{G}$. </p>
</article>